      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R1-F1",
      "reason": "The spec offered the level none but required a terminal everywhere; I now say the terminal applies at block and that none runs without one, as upgrade does."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-27T20:29:28Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R1-F2",
      "reason": "Nothing tied the confirmed digest to the writes; I added a rebuild of the whole plan just before the first write, with a refusal and no writes on any difference, and a matching acceptance criterion."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-27T20:31:09Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F1",
      "reason": "No digest was ambiguous; I now say none needs no supplied digest but still prints the one it computed, and the goal, design and criterion agree."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-27T20:31:09Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R2-F2",
      "reason": "The governing spec logs only the non-terminal route at a verified none, so I limited the logging requirement to that route and said a terminal run writes no level-log entry."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-27T20:33:09Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F1",
      "reason": "The read-only preview is a separate routed action and needs its own key; I added an agent-safe key for wb preview rerender and left writes to the rerender key."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-27T20:33:09Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F2",
      "reason": "Writing the record first could leave the record and replaced gate files agreeing while the render is half done; I reversed the order so the record is written last and any earlier failure reads as block, and changed criterion 4."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-27T20:33:09Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R3-F3",
      "reason": "An edit can land after the hash check; I added a per-file check just before the atomic replace and listed the remaining window under Limits instead of claiming it is closed."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-27T20:41:08Z",
      "choice": "applied",
      "earlier": [],
      "finding": "R4-F1",
      "reason": "The none level cannot work for this command because the level read returns block exactly when a re-render is needed; at your choice I made the command terminal-only, offering block only, and removed the none flow from the goals, design and criteria."
    }
  ],
